#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110379 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35fe6748-f040-5318-84e0-f3f76c9c7250" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "eceb2f88-2948-5037-bdbb-60483b3a2f34" :question/math-academy-id "e-3470" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\sin \\theta \\, (1 + \\cot^2 \\theta)$." :question/worked-solution "First, using the identity\n\n$$\n1 + \\cot^2 \\theta = \\csc^2 \\theta\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\sin θ(1 + \\cot^{2} θ) = \\sin θ \\cdot \\csc^{2} θ\n$$\n\nThen, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\csc {\\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sin{\\theta}}\n$$\n\nwe can further simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin θ \\cdot \\csc^{2} θ &= \\sin θ \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sin^{2} θ} \\\\\n&= \\sin θ \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sin θ \\cdot \\sin θ} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sin θ} \\\\\n&= \\csc θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110380 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "240a0a0b-fb86-5760-bb2b-74275708ff77" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "0d77018a-b39f-57f6-b2b8-646c1ed73b9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-3472" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\csc^2{\\theta} - 1}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\csc^2{\\theta} - 1 = \\cot^2{\\theta}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{\\csc^{2} θ - 1} &= \\frac{1}{\\cot^{2} θ} = \\tan^{2} θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110381 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d012a04e-f802-5a26-b900-0801427073d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "e3b17108-28ce-5a36-b211-05e6671c1f37" :question/math-academy-id "e-3473" :question/problem "Simplify $\\csc x + \\csc x \\cot^2 x -\\csc^3x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\csc x$ from the first two terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\csc x + \\csc x\\cot^{2} x - \\csc^{3} x &= \\csc x(1 + \\cot^{2} x) - \\csc^{3} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the cotangent-cosecant identity,\n\n$$\n1+ \\cot^2 x=\\csc^2 x\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\csc x(1 + \\cot^{2} x) - \\csc^{3} x &= \\csc x \\cdot (\\csc^{2} x) - \\csc^{3} x \\\\\n&= \\csc^{3} x - \\csc^{3} x \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110386 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85555bce-debf-5165-ba6a-3c232deeeb0a" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "4da93c71-9a1e-512e-9735-14d7c6221378" :question/math-academy-id "e-3497" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\csc \\theta + \\cot \\theta} + \\cot \\theta$." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n1= \\csc^2{\\theta} -\\cot^2{\\theta}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{\\csc θ + \\cot θ} + \\cot θ &= \\frac{\\csc^{2} θ - \\cot^{2} θ}{\\csc θ + \\cot θ} + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= ((\\csc θ - \\cot θ)(\\csc θ + \\cot θ))/(\\csc θ + \\cot θ) + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= ((\\csc θ - \\cot θ)(\\csc θ + \\cot θ))/(\\csc θ + \\cot θ) + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= (\\csc θ - \\cot θ) + \\cot θ \\\\\n&= \\csc θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35fe6748-f040-5318-84e0-f3f76c9c7250" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d48e5d0-98b8-5475-bed0-edeb7a789b3a" :answer/type {